# Ready for Another Tree?

@body

- Work on the second handout after you finish the class example.
- It uses the same six labels with different distances.
- Check your sheet: a-b is 11 and d-f is 6.
- Build the tree and label every branch length.
- Try it before looking at the following answers.

=== layout: subsection

# Extension Problem: Answers

=== include: gene_tree_six_extension_steps.djot

=== layout: bookend

# Key Takeaways

@body

- Join the closest clusters and update the matrix after each merge.
- Use half the join distance for the new node height.
- Subtract child height from parent height for each branch.
- Compare distances along tree paths with the original distances.

